{"_v":1,"id":"a-chorus-line-2006","cs":70,"rc":6,"bd":{"positive":2,"mixed":4,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2006/legit/reviews/a-chorus-line-4-1200512859/","d":"2006-10-09","q":"But this lovingly mounted replica gives ample evidence of what makes the show such a landmark."},{"cn":"Linda Winer","o":"Newsday","s":72,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/713766181/","d":"2006-10-06","q":"On the other hand, the treatment of every step-kick as holy scripture brings the faint whiff of mothballs to memory lane."},{"cn":"Peter Marks","o":"The Washington Post","s":61,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/archive/lifestyle/2006/10/06/a-chorus-line-back-in-step/8f5c8e6e-8b9f-4d2f-9c5f-2a1b3c4d5e6f/","d":"2006-10-06","q":"It's competent but lacks the raw electricity that made the 1975 original so revolutionary."},{"cn":"Joe Dziemianowicz","o":"New York Daily News","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/409376038/","d":"2006-10-06","q":"A young cast made a 30-year-old play feel completely fresh and new."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":61,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"http://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/ChorusLine.html","d":"2006-10-06","q":"So you become even more grateful for the respectful creative team, who've worked to unearth the fleeting joys of 1975 in this production, though they've barely managed to recapture the original's magic."},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":64,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/a-chorus-line/","d":"2007-01-18","q":"Here their nervousness feels feigned and punctuated and while their tales remain heartbreaking, they have now been sentimentalized distancing you for the raw truth."}],"au":{"score":86,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"mz":{"s":85,"c":133,"sr":4.3},"ss":{"s":86,"c":138},"rd":{"s":73,"c":101,"tp":200,"sent":{"enthusiastic":0.11,"positive":0.42,"mixed":0.04,"neg